<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Consulta of Lyon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1801–1802</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Consulta di Lione</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Consulta of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lyon">Lyon</a> was an assembly of some 450 delegates of the Cisalpine Republic convened by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon Bonaparte</a> at Lyon from December 1801 to January 1802. It adopted a new constitution, transformed the Cisalpine into the Italian Republic and elected Napoleon its president, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francesco-melzi-deril">Francesco Melzi d'Eril</a> as vice-president. It was a step towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a> proclaimed in 1805.</p></div>
